# No Cursor / AI attribution

Never add product or tool branding to git commits, pull request bodies, issue comments, release notes, or changelogs.

Forbidden examples (do not write these or similar):

- `Made with Cursor`
- `Co-authored-by: Cursor` / `Co-authored-by: CursorAgent`
- `Generated-by: Cursor`, `Built with Cursor`, `Created with AI`
- Footers, signatures, or markdown horizontal rules whose purpose is tool attribution

Write commit messages and PR text as normal human-authored project contributions.

When the user asks to **git commit** or **push**, use the `commit-attribution` skill (`git commit-tree` / `git-commit-clean.sh`), not plain `git commit`, and verify `git log -1 --format=%B` has no Cursor co-author trailers before push.

When opening PRs with `gh pr create`, pass a clean body only — no attribution footer.
